# THIS FILE IS NOT ENFORCED. Branch protection on `main` is not configured
# (removed 2026-10-22 — see ci/README.md §13): this is a single-owner
# repository, so a required code-owner review could never be satisfied (the
# sole owner cannot approve their own change) and the required `woodpecker`
# commit-status context was posted by nothing. GitHub therefore does not gate
# on this file today.
#
# What it is still good for: it names the owner of each area, so a future
# reviewer, an auditor, or a second maintainer can see who is responsible
# without reading the tree. Keep it current as a routing document.
#
# SINGLE-POINT-OF-OWNERSHIP RISK (unchanged, and real): every path below is
# owned by the same account that authors every commit. If this repository
# ever gains a second maintainer, add them to the release-critical paths —
# /ci/, /deploy/, .woodpecker.yml — AND enable protection as a set (a CI that
# posts the required status, a non-author code owner, enforce_admins: true).
# Until then, treat CI/release changes as self-reviewed and rely on the
# mechanical gates instead: the validate stage's pipeline-config sanity
# checks, the digest-pinned executor image, and the blessing manifest whose
# pipelineConfigHash covers every gate script.

